{"chapter": "moduli", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "0DM1", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-quot}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ebe2adb064be3f04c80995f9704aaa0b0cb1959f85d302b34e5519e81dd9b081", "source_text": "Properties of Quot", "source_text_hash": "sha256:449a7fa561872ec4fe349e318eb85a6fbacd96e0d9d96fc6e0fdf09b22ab5559", "unit_id": "tag:0DM1:title"}
{"chapter": "moduli", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0DM1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to B$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\Quotfunctor_{\\mathcal{F}/X/B}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\Quotfunctor_{\\mathcal{F}/X/B} \\to B$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{quot-proposition-quot}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:f15a024c0eac833272f7b45c640e849723840bbe6a08a460dace4999fb8d9d44", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8bfebc583fc39ec4f1ae702d7741a333d7b98cd35f91fbf8e8f8a64071bee15c", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a morphism of algebraic spaces which is\nseparated and of finite presentation. Let <MATH_0002> be a\nquasi-coherent <MATH_0003>-module. Then\n<MATH_0004> is an algebraic space.\nIf <MATH_0005> is of finite presentation, then\n<MATH_0006> is locally of finite\npresentation. See Quot, Proposition <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:139e1173071fd40de034f28a3616fefa63d12914a0db7a0f30cb91244dbe8aac", "unit_id": "tag:0DM1:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "moduli", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0DM1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\Quotfunctor_{\\mathcal{F}/X/B} \\to B$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-quot-diagonal-closed}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:865f25d89d93ad7baa466e93f99715eb300568998a52617e21b8d44568a12560", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:01374f802bbe1f8112d4f91d065bbe1cca4fbc9eadfcf05ff69c937e10a4720c", "source_text": "The diagonal of <MATH_0001> is a closed immersion.\nIf <MATH_0002> is of finite type, then the diagonal is a closed\nimmersion of finite presentation.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b13cff0750a3b1ff8ec4239757a6434cf1cb9c3517d6821572784b165d959a6a", "unit_id": "tag:0DM2:statement"}
{"chapter": "moduli", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0DM1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$T/B$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}_T \\to \\mathcal{Q}_i$", "MATH_0003": "$i = 1, 2$", "MATH_0004": "$T$", "MATH_0005": "$\\Quotfunctor_{\\mathcal{F}/X/B}$", "MATH_0006": "$B$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{K}_1$", "MATH_0008": "$u : \\mathcal{K}_1 \\to \\mathcal{Q}_2$", "MATH_0009": "$T$", "MATH_0010": "$T' \\to T$", "MATH_0011": "$u_{T'}$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0013": "$\\mathcal{K}_1$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-flat-lemma-F-zero-closed-proper}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{sites-modules-lemma-kernel-surjection-finite-onto-finite-presentation}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ab5b59702841a569b738d98ba05569809f8d1e15e42a8ccef4f15c92a4744db3", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9d8c36ecd866b9a1442daad8947ed791f87737776c2085a2ee8790f9935b1c4b", "source_text": "Suppose we have a scheme <MATH_0001> and two quotients\n<MATH_0002>, <MATH_0003> corresponding\nto <MATH_0004>-valued points of <MATH_0005> over <MATH_0006>.\nDenote <MATH_0007> the kernel of the first one and set\n<MATH_0008> the composition.\nBy Flatness on Spaces, Lemma <REF_0001>\nthere is a closed subspace of <MATH_0009> such that <MATH_0010>\nfactors through it if and only if the pullback <MATH_0011> is zero.\nThis proves the diagonal is a closed immersion.\nMoreover, if <MATH_0012> is of finite type, then\n<MATH_0013> is of finite type\n(Modules on Sites, Lemma\n<REF_0002>)\nand we see that the diagonal is of finite presentation by\nthe same lemma.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7a057ef888aefb4df0ee1783444eab124bd3229598f1ce9cac8ae8e186a9e455", "unit_id": "tag:0DM2:proof"}
{"chapter": "moduli", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0DM1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\Quotfunctor_{\\mathcal{F}/X/B} \\to B$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-quot-s-lfp}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:865f25d89d93ad7baa466e93f99715eb300568998a52617e21b8d44568a12560", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5c279e2d307176fac99d15bc86d642796cfc92a06e595fb3bc8c2a85ce318c47", "source_text": "The morphism <MATH_0001> is separated.\nIf <MATH_0002> is of finite presentation, then it is also\nlocally of finite presentation.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c655e33431212204aebbce8f3626569713b67f6f8d0967b687253c9dfb0d5da3", "unit_id": "tag:0DM3:statement"}
